    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d685">

                <pb facs="0957" n="855" sameAs="frus:frus1933v01/pg855"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 Czechoslovakia/215</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Moley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-06-12">June 12, 1933</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Czechoslovak Minister called to consult me with regard to the payment of the
                    installment in silver and I laid down the following rule to be followed in
                    connection with this payment and payments of a similar nature from other
                    countries. Under the terms of An Act, Public, Number 10, 73rd Congress, House
                    Roll 3835, Title Number 3, Section 45, approved May 12, 1933,<anchor n="55"
                        xml:id="d685-f1"/> the President has authorized me to say to the
                    representatives of those countries who desire to pay all or part of their
                    installments in silver, that he will accept silver at fifty cents an ounce. I
                    stated further that it was our policy not to indicate where the silver should be
                    purchased or at what price.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Raymond Moley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
